    "preamble": "Annapoorna Vanitha Canteen vs Dr.V.S.Sajeev on 13 March, 2017 Author: Shaji P. Chaly Bench: Shaji P.Chaly In The High Court Of Kerala At Ernakulam Present: The Honourable Mr. Justice Shaji P.Chaly Monday, The 7Th Day Of August 2017/16Th Sravana, 1939 Con.Case(C).No. 905 of 2017 (S) ------------------------------- Interim Order In Wp(C) 39634/2016 Dated 13-03-2017. .......",
    "facts": "This contempt case is filed by the petitioner complaining that the interim order passed by this Court in W.P.(C). An affidavit is filed by the Annapoorna Vanitha Canteen vs Dr.V.S.Sajeev on 13 March, 2017 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/110146117/ 2 respondent and among other contentions it is stated that the license from the Municipality is obtained by the contractor on 20.06.2017. Today when the matter is taken up, learned Government Pleader has also produced the license issued by the concerned authority under the Food Safety and Standards Act.",
